    <bpmn:process id="W_W3370" name="W3370. Corporate Positioning &amp; Stakeholder Narrative Development" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual; strategy refresh; complements VS-14.3 brand
Frequency: Annual + on change
Volume: Corporate narrative
Owner: Government Affairs Manager
Participants: Govt Affairs Mgr, Comms/Brand (links to VS-14.3), Strategy (links to VS-33), Leadership, ESG (links to VS-25.2)
Source: workflow W3370 — Corporate Positioning &amp; Stakeholder Narrative Development</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3370_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3370_Lane1" name="Govt Affairs Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3370_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3370_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3370_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3370_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3370_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3370_Start3" name="Annual; strategy refresh; complements VS-14.3 brand">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3370_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3370_Task4" name="Govt Affairs Mgr/Comms develop BuildRight&#x27;s corporate positioning and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Govt Affairs Mgr/Comms develop BuildRight&#x27;s corporate positioning and stakeholder narrative for external-affairs audiences: purpose, economic contribution (jobs, tax, suppliers), sustainability (links to VS-25), community impact, and policy stance
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs Mgr / Comms
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3370_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3370_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3370_Task5" name="Govt Affairs Mgr tailor the narrative to audiences (government, industry…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Govt Affairs Mgr tailor the narrative to audiences (government, industry, community, media, investors) and align with brand/PR (links to VS-14.3) and ESG reporting (links to VS-25.2); train spokespeople
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs Mgr / Comms
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3370_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3370_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3370_Task6" name="Govt Affairs Mgr monitor stakeholder perception and reputation (surveys, media…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Govt Affairs Mgr monitor stakeholder perception and reputation (surveys, media sentiment, social), measure narrative resonance, and refine positioning
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3370_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3370_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3370_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3370_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3370_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-543 (ensure controlled execution — Public Affairs, Community Relations &amp; Reputation (PA-104.3).) | - operational: authenticity and ESG substance; operational: monitoring
Owner: Government Affairs Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
