      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3374_Task4" name="Govt Affairs Mgr/Risk assess political and regulatory risks: policy/legislative…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Govt Affairs Mgr/Risk assess political and regulatory risks: policy/legislative shifts (tax reform, retail regulation, labor, payments, data, customs/tariff links to VS-87), political instability, elections, geopolitical/supply-chain risk; estimate likelihood/impact
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs Mgr / Risk
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3374_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3374_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3374_Task5" name="Govt Affairs Mgr/Risk develop mitigation strategies (advocacy W3355, compliance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Govt Affairs Mgr/Risk develop mitigation strategies (advocacy W3355, compliance readiness links to VS-22.3, scenario/contingency planning links to VS-26 BCP, supply-chain resilience links to VS-02.3); integrate into the enterprise risk register (links to VS-21.2)
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs Mgr / Risk
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3374_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3374_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3374_Task6" name="Govt Affairs Mgr monitor risk indicators, update assessments as the environment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Govt Affairs Mgr monitor risk indicators, update assessments as the environment changes, and report political/regulatory risk to leadership and the board/audit committee (links to VS-21/VS-36)
Responsible (R): Govt Affairs Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3374_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3374_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
